^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.* does not uniquely resolve:
--
Verifies that an unqualified call to a static member function from
inside a derived class resolves to the derived-class member when the
inherited base-class member has the same signature, even if one of the
arguments has a class type whose declaring class also defines the same
name.  This is [class.member.lookup]/4 (name hiding by derived class)
applied after CBMC's broad ADL gather step in `resolve_with_arguments`.
